  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The extraction principle used in extraction of a metal 'M' can be represented as follows<br />\r<br />\r<math> <mrow> <mtable> <mtr> <mtd> <mtext>MS</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>O</mtext> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>→</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <msub> <mtext>MSO</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <msub> <mtext>MSO</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>MS</mtext> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>→</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>M</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>SO</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable> </mrow> </math><br />\r<br />\rThe metal 'M' is</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Mg",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Pb",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Sn",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "It is a case of self reduction.<br><br>The concentrated galena (PbS) is partially oxidised by adjusting the air supply.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>PbS</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>→</mo> <msub> <mtext>PbSO</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math><br /><br />The temperature is raised, air supply reduced and fresh galena (PbS) added.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>PbS</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mtext>PbSO</mtext> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <mo>→</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>Pb</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>SO</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>↑</mo> </mrow> </math>"
  }
